<article class="env-proposition" id="06WG">
<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/06WG">Proposition <span data-tag="06WG">9.6.6.18</span>.</a> Let $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ be an $\infty $-category containing morphisms $f: A \rightarrow B$ and $g: X \rightarrow Y$. Then the (strictly commutative) diagram of Kan complexes </p>
<div class="equation" id="06WH">
<span class="equation-label"><a data-tag="06WH" href="/tag/06WH">9.35</a></span>
<div>\begin{equation}  \begin{gathered}\label{equation:diagram-describing-orthogonality-concrete} \xymatrix@R =50pt@C=50pt{ _{f}\operatorname{Hom}_{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}}(A,B,X,Y)_{g} \ar [r] \ar [d] &amp;  \operatorname{Hom}_{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}}(A,X,Y)_{g} \ar [d] \\ _{f}\operatorname{Hom}_{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}}(A,B,Y) \ar [r] &amp;  \operatorname{Hom}_{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}}(A,Y) } \end{gathered} \end{equation}</div>
</div>
<p> determines a diagram $\Delta ^1 \times \Delta ^1 \rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{S}}$, which is isomorphic to the diagram (<a data-tag="06W4" href="/tag/06W4">9.32</a>) appearing in Definition <a data-tag="04NN" href="/tag/04NN">9.6.6.1</a>. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
<p>
<strong>Proof of Proposition <a data-tag="06WG" href="/tag/06WG">9.6.6.18</a>.</strong>
       Let $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ be an $\infty $-category and let $f: A \rightarrow B$ and $g: X \rightarrow Y$ be morphisms of $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$. Set $J = \Delta ^1 = K$, so that $f$ and $g$ can be identified with diagrams $F: J \rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ and $G: K \rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$, respectively. The diagram 
    <p>
<div class="equation" id="06WQ">
<span class="equation-label"><a data-tag="06WQ" href="/tag/06WQ">9.38</a></span>
<div>\begin{equation}  \begin{gathered}\label{equation:concrete-model-for-Hom} \xymatrix@R =50pt@C=50pt{ \operatorname{Hom}_{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}}(B,X) \ar [r] \ar [d] &amp;  \operatorname{Hom}_{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}}(A,X) \ar [d] \\ \operatorname{Hom}_{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}}( B, Y) \ar [r] &amp;  \operatorname{Hom}_{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}}(A, Y) } \end{gathered} \end{equation}</div>
</div>
<p>
       appearing in Definition <a data-tag="04NN" href="/tag/04NN">9.6.6.1</a> is characterized, up to isomorphism in $\operatorname{Fun}( \Delta ^1 \times \Delta ^1, \operatorname{\mathcal{S}})$, by the requirement that it is a covariant transport representation for the left fibration 
    <p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  U: J^{\operatorname{op}} \times _{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}^{\operatorname{op}} } \operatorname{Tw}(\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}) \times _{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}} K \rightarrow J^{\operatorname{op}} \times K. \]
</div>
<p>
       Since $J^{\operatorname{op}} \times K$ is (the nerve of) an ordinary category, we can identify (<a data-tag="06WQ" href="/tag/06WQ">9.38</a>) with the (strictly) commutative diagram of Kan complexes obtained from the strict transport representation of Construction <a data-tag="035J" href="/tag/035J">5.3.1.5</a> (Example <a data-tag="0386" href="/tag/0386">5.6.5.7</a>). Setting $J_0 = \{ 0\}  \subseteq J$ and $K_0 = \{ 1\}  \subseteq K$, this diagram is given by 
    <p>
<div class="equation" id="06WR">
<span class="equation-label"><a data-tag="06WR" href="/tag/06WR">9.39</a></span>
<div>\begin{equation}  \begin{gathered}\label{equation:concrete-model-for-Hom2} \xymatrix@R =50pt@C=50pt{ \operatorname{Fun}_{ / \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}^{\operatorname{op}} \times \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}}( J^{\operatorname{op}} \times K, \operatorname{Tw}(\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}) ) \ar [r] \ar [d] &amp;  \operatorname{Fun}_{ / \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}^{\operatorname{op}} \times \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}}( J^{\operatorname{op}}_{0} \times K, \operatorname{Tw}(\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}) ) \ar [d] \\ \operatorname{Fun}_{ / \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}^{\operatorname{op}} \times \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}}( J^{\operatorname{op}} \times K_0, \operatorname{Tw}(\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}) ) \ar [r] &amp;  \operatorname{Fun}_{ / \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}^{\operatorname{op}} \times \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}}( J^{\operatorname{op}}_0 \times K_0, \operatorname{Tw}(\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}) ).} \end{gathered} \end{equation}</div>
</div>
<p>
       Applying Notation <a data-tag="06WP" href="/tag/06WP">9.6.6.27</a>, we obtain an equivalence to (<a data-tag="06WR" href="/tag/06WR">9.39</a>) from the diagram of Kan complexes 
    <p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix@R =50pt@C=50pt{ \operatorname{Fun}_{/\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}}( K, \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_{f/} ) \ar [r] \ar [d] &amp;  \operatorname{Fun}_{ / \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}}( K, \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_{A/} ) \ar [d] \\ \operatorname{Fun}_{ / \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}}( K_0, \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_{f/} ) \ar [r] &amp;  \operatorname{Fun}_{ / \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}}( K_0, \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_{A/} ), } \]
</div>
<p>
       which in turn admits an equivalence to the diagram 
    <p>
<div class="equation">
  \[ \xymatrix@R =50pt@C=50pt{ _{f}\operatorname{Hom}_{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}}(A,B,X,Y)_{g} \ar [r] \ar [d] &amp;  \operatorname{Hom}_{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}}(A,X,Y)_{g} \ar [d] \\ _{f}\operatorname{Hom}_{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}}(A,B,Y) \ar [r] &amp;  \operatorname{Hom}_{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}}(A,Y) } \]
</div>
<p>
       appearing in the statement of Proposition <a data-tag="06WG" href="/tag/06WG">9.6.6.18</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
</p>
